# Vallamkali CrewSync - Packet Protocol

This document defines how data moves between all devices.

Nobody should change these packet structures without informing the team.

---

# 1. MotionPacket

MotionPacket carries movement data from each wearable rower node.

## Packet Structure

```text
rower_id
sequence
timestamp

ax
ay
az

gx
gy
gz
Field Description
rower_id

Identifies the wearable band.

Example:

1 = Rower 1
2 = Rower 2
3 = Rower 3
sequence

Packet number.

Example:

1
2
3
4
5

Used to detect missing packets.

timestamp

Time when the sensor data was collected.

Used to compare movement timing.

ax, ay, az

Accelerometer values from the IMU.

These represent movement acceleration on the X, Y and Z axes.

gx, gy, gz

Gyroscope values from the IMU.

These represent rotational movement on the X, Y and Z axes.

Motion Data Flow
IMU
 ↓
Wearable ESP32
 ↓
MotionPacket
 ↓
ESP-NOW
 ↓
Central ESP32
 ↓
Raspberry Pi
2. FeedbackPacket

FeedbackPacket carries the AI decision back to a wearable band.

Packet Structure
target_rower
status
error_type
intensity
duration
Field Description
target_rower

Identifies which wearable should receive feedback.

Example:

1
2
3
status

Current synchronization state.

Possible values:

SYNC
WARNING
OUT_OF_SYNC
error_type

Describes the detected problem.

Possible values:

TOO_FAST
TOO_SLOW
EARLY_STROKE
LATE_STROKE
IRREGULAR_MOTION
intensity

Strength of vibration feedback.

Example:

0 = OFF
1 = LOW
2 = MEDIUM
3 = HIGH
duration

How long the vibration should operate.

Example:

200 ms
500 ms
1000 ms
Feedback Flow
Gemma AI
 ↓
Raspberry Pi
 ↓
FeedbackPacket
 ↓
Central ESP32
 ↓
ESP-NOW
 ↓
Target Wearable
 ↓
LED + Vibration
